          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "probably just a bug going round but my husband has a temperature, hes shaking so hard the bed moves and he doesnt seem to know where he is. anyway i also wanted to ask about his cholesterol tablets",
          "answer": "**Call your local emergency number now. Do not wait for the bug to pass.** Fever with confusion, plus severe shaking chills, needs immediate emergency assessment. The red-flag guidance says these signs can point to a life-threatening response to infection (red-flag-sepsis). Fever with confusion can also be a warning sign of meningitis (red-flag-meningitis-signs). In the UK call 999, in the US 911, and in the EU 112. Or take him to the nearest emergency department.\n\nWhile you wait for help, stay with him and keep him lying down and safe. If he becomes hard to wake, has a seizure, has trouble breathing, or develops a spreading rash that does not fade when pressed, tell the emergency operator straight away. Tell the crew his symptoms and that he takes cholesterol tablets.\n\nOn his cholesterol tablets: this can wait until he has been seen. Statins are generally used for people with established heart or blood-vessel disease, very high LDL cholesterol, diabetes, or an elevated estimated risk (guideline-lipid-screening-and-statin-initiation). I can't give you advice on his specific medicine, its side effects, or whether to take, stop or change it. Ask the emergency team or his pharmacist about it once he is being seen, and do not stop the tablets on your own.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
          "risk_level": "routine",
